/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# bench artifacts (fixtures are fetched, not committed)
/bench/fixtures/repos
/bench/fixtures/artifacts
*.stats.json
*.js.map

# bench/results/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those files are the evidence
# trail: every number in the docs cites one, and a measurement nobody can
# inspect is a claim. They are a few KB each because the raw fixtures are not
# committed - the results record the fixture's parameters, not its bytes.

# local caches
.nopeat-cache/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
dist/
report*.html
*-report.html

# mdbook build output. The sources under docs/ are versioned - that is the
# point of restoring the book - only what `mdbook build` generates is not.
book/

# webpack-bundle-analyzer's raw json export: written by every parity run, and it is
# the reference tool's output, not a record of ours.
bench/results/parity-wba.json

# docs/ is the mdbook source tree: prose, assets and schema contracts are all
# versioned, because `mdbook build` fails on a SUMMARY entry whose file is
# missing and a book that only builds on the maintainer's machine is not a book.
# The one exception is the last entry in this file.

history-rewrite-report.md
aiscan_tmp.py

# The only file under docs/ that is not published: the curated issue list, which
# is a working document rather than a document anyone reads. It is gitignored
# rather than deleted because it is kept up to date and pushed to GitHub by hand
# once it is ready.
docs/good-first-issues.md
